[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Who moves a DECISION from open to accepted, and how

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[SPIKE]
UID: SPIKE-DECISION-ACCEPTANCE-PATH
TITLE: Who moves a DECISION from open to accepted, and how
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: run
RETIRES_ON: >>>
The first open-to-accepted transition is made on this branch with its actor
and its trigger recorded, or the README states the path outright.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
No open-to-accepted transition has ever occurred on this branch: every
accepted decision was born accepted, and the one exit from open was
open-to-superseded. The README says a planning session grooms, decides and
slots, and also that decisions come to the operator as plain-language cards;
the skill does not say who turns STATUS. DEC-LONG-LIVED-BRANCH's acceptance
language is about signing, not STATUS. The transition drawn in every state
machine is inferred from the enum, not observed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A transition that exists only in the enum is the kind of gate that gets
guessed at. Observing it once settles who owns it.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
RUN 2026-08-27, by observation rather than by probe. The operator stated the
path outright, which is this spike's second retirement arm.

WHO: the operator. HOW: in conversation, ad hoc. There is no gate, no trigger
and no form, and that is deliberate while the system is being dogfooded. In
their words: "We are making it up as you go, pretend dog fooding its a good
system."

Record it plainly and do not build ceremony around it. This spike's own
rationale is that a transition existing only in the enum "is the kind of gate
that gets guessed at", so the value of the answer is that it stops the next
session inventing one.

Do NOT read this as covering fingerprint signing. This spike already drew that
line -- DEC-LONG-LIVED-BRANCH's acceptance language is about signing, not STATUS
-- and that decision is unchanged: two reviews, the stack reviewed whole for
usability and flow, the pull requests reviewed for implementation choices, and
operator acceptance turned at the second of these, never before. STATUS is
conversational; signing waits for the pull request.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-LONG-LIVED-BRANCH
  ROLE: Governed_By
